From 0100387cf5db996b4f2ac3f1b9e746e1fc6a8835 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fra <fra@localhost>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 11:49:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 01/13] fix: start airouter with provider API keys in its
 environment
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

systemd's EnvironmentFile= is not a shell parser: it reads KEY=value lines
and silently ignores the `export KEY=value` form direnv writes, so pointing
it at .envrc imported zero variables with no warning. Every provider call
then failed 401 and the model 401s sat in cooldowns.json for up to 168h.

Add scripts/run-airouter.sh, which sources .envrc under `set -a` (which also
resolves intra-file references like CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=$CF_API_KEY) and
execs the daemon so systemd keeps the real PID. It fails closed when .envrc
is missing, because starting without credentials looks like it works (the
daemon starts, /v1/models responds) while every provider call 401s.

Also stop model_utils.py pointing its enrichment cache at
free-models-cache.json, which is the --save target for the full model LIST
(a JSON array) — load_cache() raised AttributeError on every sync and it
surfaced as an opaque "airouter-model-sync.service failed". Degrade to a
refetch on any malformed cache instead of crashing.
---
