From d8342155863b7a9f33cdf434913a7aa0456fd738 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fra <fra@localhost>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 12:11:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 06/13] test: cover the mid-stream fallback [DONE] path and add
 an SSE integrity harness
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Closes the remaining under-tested branch of the stream-truncation bug class.

The existing TestProviderProxyStreamingMidStreamResume drives the proxy
fallback loop by hand, so it never exercises handleStream's deferred
sendDone(). Added two gateway-level tests that go through the real
HandleChatCompletions path and assert the termination contract on the bytes
the client actually receives:

  TestHandleStream_MidStreamFallbackEmitsDoneOnce — attempt 1 flushes content
    then an SSE error; attempt 2 completes. Every streamSSE call emits its own
    sentinel, so the question is whether a further one stacks on top.
  TestHandleStream_UpstreamClosesWithoutDoneAcrossFallback — same, with
    attempt 1 killed mid-stream and no sentinel at all.

Both verified to fail when the sentinel emission is removed, so they are not
vacuous.

TestSSEEventIsRelease_FailOpen pins the deliberate fail-open behaviour of the
release predicate. Failing open is what keeps an unrecognised event shape from
stalling the stream forever, but it is also what made the `: keepalive` bug
destructive, so the correct fix was to keep comments out of the event path —
not to make the predicate fail-closed. Without this test someone may
"tighten" it and silently reintroduce truncation.

scripts/sse-check.py turns the contract into a routine assertion against a
running gateway: exactly one sentinel, last, no leaked comments, content
reassembles. It separates framing violations (FAIL) from contentless streams
(warn), because reasoning models like kilocode/dots-studio can spend an entire
max_tokens budget on a reasoning trace and emit no content — a provider
problem, not a gateway bug, and reporting it as truncation sends you hunting
for a bug that isn't there. Verified it flags a simulated pre-fix gateway
(double sentinel, leading sentinel, leaked keepalive) and exits non-zero.

.github/workflows/ci.yml gates gofmt, go vet, go test -race, config
validation, the generator regression tests, and a py_compile pass, so the
gofmt drift just closed cannot silently return.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
