From 1943655d182b650267c4d881c1694572cca2601d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fra <fra@localhost>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 12:55:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 08/13] feat: mount /metrics, add attempt telemetry, and assert
 the SSE contract in CI
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three defects, one of them long-hidden.

/metrics was implemented but never registered in the mux, so it 404'd in every
deployment and the whole Metrics collector was dead code — while the RUNBOOK
claimed the handler was "wired into all four request surfaces". It also
performed no authentication while exposing provider/model-labelled routing
telemetry. Now mounted and gated behind checkAuth, pinned by tests and by a CI
assertion that an unauthenticated scrape is refused.

streamSSE wrote the event that triggers the release *before* the buffer it
belongs behind, so clients received role=assistant after their first content
token — inverting SSE delta ordering, which reads as two responses. Fixed by
flushing the buffer inside the release branch, pinned twice: by a byte-offset
test and by a wire-level test that parses the emitted SSE and asserts the
contract independently of how buffering is implemented.

Also:
- add per-endpoint attempt latency/outcome metrics and an
  airouter_sse_comments_routed_out canary, wired through the shared collector
- bound all five fallback loops with a shared budgetState, including the
  WebSocket turn loop that the structural test caught shipping unbounded
- fix per-attempt timer shadowing that made recordRequest measure only the
  final attempt
- untrack runtime state files already in .gitignore
- add the sse-contract CI job (fake upstream + booted gateway, no provider
  credentials needed) asserting the termination contract, and assert the
  metrics are present AND non-zero so they cannot go dead unnoticed again
- resolve every OPEN item in docs/audit.md to FIXED or ACCEPTED with rationale,
  and record the reading convention for the stale line-number citations
