+  # End-to-end assertion of the SSE termination contract. The bug this guards
+  # (a `data: [DONE]` released ahead of the real chunks, so the client silently
+  # drops the answer) returned HTTP 200 and was invisible to every check in the
+  # go job — it only shows up when you assert on the captured bytes. That is
+  # what scripts/sse-check.py does, so it needs a real gateway in front of a
+  # real SSE stream.
