+  # The upstream is scripts/fake-sse-upstream.py, not a live provider: CI has no
+  # provider credentials, and the contract is decided by the gateway's framing,
+  # not by which model answered. The fake is deliberately nastier than a real
+  # provider (comment lines interleaved mid-chunk, no trailing blank line on the
+  # final event) so the test actually exercises the failure modes.
